The first projection of Proposition 6.2 is the approximable map from the product of A and B to A that relates a consistent product set u to a consistent set v of A exactly when A entails v from the first projection of u. The domain and codomain of a related pair are those two consistency hypotheses. The empty set is related because the empty product set is consistent, the empty set of A is consistent, and the first projection of the empty product set is empty, which entails the empty set. The relation is closed under union on the right by proposition 2.3(vi) for the entailment and by proposition 2.3(ii) together with the subset axiom for consistency of the union. It is monotone by two applications of proposition 2.3(iv), using that product entailment projects to entailment of first projections.
